# The rendered Service Area Register is INTERNAL ANALYSIS, not client-facing work: it
# documents defects in the client's own live site (duplicate pages, a competitor mention,
# a ChatGPT tracking artefact, coverage claims that exceed what they publish). The repo is
# the public preview, so publishing it there would put that analysis on a URL the client's
# own team browses. The DATA and the generators stay committed so it is reproducible with
# one command; only the rendered page is withheld. It is already published privately as an
# Artifact for the owner.
